1. **A pistol comprising:**  
   a frame;  
   a reciprocating slide movable relative to the frame between a forward battery position and a rearward retracted position, the slide including a breech portion;  
   a magazine configured to feed cartridges toward the breech portion;  
   a cartridge feeder disposed in the magazine and biased toward a feed position; and  
   a breech hold-open mechanism including a catch pivotably supported relative to the frame, the catch having a locking portion and a projection engageable by the cartridge feeder;  
   **wherein**, upon depletion of cartridges from the magazine, the cartridge feeder advances into engagement with the projection and pivots the catch from a non-locking position to a locking position, and  
   **wherein**, in the locking position, the locking portion of the catch engages a cooperating surface of the slide to retain the slide in the rearward retracted position.
